  "summaries": [
    {
      "id": 921472,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "`ActionText::Content#to_markdown` writes the text of `<code>` and `<pre>` elements unescaped and relies on the code span delimiter to keep it inert. For code in a table cell that starts with two or more spaces or a tab, such as `<td><code>  [click](javascript:alert(1))</code></td>`, it emitted a code span delimited by two backticks. That Markdown is correct, and Commonmarker and Redcarpet render it as code. kramdown rebuilds the span with a single backtick when it splits the table row into cells, then fails to open it, and renders a `javascript:` link that `to_markdown` refuses to emit from an `<a>` element.\n\nWe closed the report as Informative because the link comes from kramdown misparsing correct Markdown. We changed `to_markdown` in [rails/rails#58956](https://github.com/rails/rails/pull/58956) to strip leading and trailing whitespace from code spans in table cells, which avoids the kramdown behavior. `to_markdown` is not yet in any released version of Rails.\n\nThanks to @deah313 for the report.\n",
